{
  "title": "Anterior Superior Iliac Spine (ASIS) Avulsion",
  "url": "https://www.orthobullets.com/knee-and-sports/3091/anterior-superior-iliac-spine-asis-avulsion",
  "subtitle": "Updated: Apr 29 2023",
  "sections": [
    {
      "text": "summary",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "3",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "An anterior superior iliac spine (ASIS) avulsion is a traumatic avulsion of the ASIS due to a sudden and forceful contraction of the sartorius and tensor fascia lata that occurs in young athletes.",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "4",
          "children": []
        },
        {
          "text": "Diagnosis is made radiographically with displaced injuries but CT/MRI may be required to diagnosis nondisplaced fractures.",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "-1",
          "children": []
        },
        {
          "text": "Treatment is nonoperative for fractures < 3 cm displacement with rest and protected weight bearing. Surgical treatment is indicated for fractures > 3 cm displaced.",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "-1",
          "children": []
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Etiology",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "-1",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Mechanism",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "result from indirect trauma",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "caused by **sudden and forceful** contraction of **sartorius** and **tensor fascia lata**",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "5",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "occurs during **hip extension** (sprinting or swinging a baseball bat)",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "4",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Anatomy",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "3",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Muscles that originate from ASIS",
          "table": null,
          "images": [
            {
              "src": "https://upload.orthobullets.com/topic/3091/images/avulsionillustration_moved.jpg",
              "caption": ""
            }
          ],
          "importance": "1",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "sartorius (femoral n.)",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "1",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "tensor fascia lata (superior gluteal n.)",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "1",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Presentation",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "3",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "History",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "athlete will often report a **pop or snap** at the time of injury",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "4",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Symptoms",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "may complain of weakness",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "may be confused or misdiagnosed as an acute muscle strain",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "3",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Physical exam",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "may see weakness to hip flexion and knee extension",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "severe injuries may result in a limp",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Imaging",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "3",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Radiographs",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "displaced fractures usually can be seen on radiographs",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "may be missed due to location and small size of bony fragment",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "3",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "CT or MRI",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "can be obtained to confirm the diagnosis",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Treatment",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "3",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Nonoperative",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "rest, protected weight bearing with crutches, and early ROM and stretching",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "5",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "indications",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "5",
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "text": "most cases",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "4",
                      "children": []
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Operative",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "ORIF of avulsion fracture",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "4",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "indications",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "1",
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "text": "fractures with **displacement of > 3 cm**",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "4",
                      "children": []
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "painful nonunions",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
